      "message": "sorry for the delay on replying here.\n\nreturn all vs return none is not what the API spec says for the subtree_as_list param: https://github.com/openstack/keystone-specs/blob/master/api/v3/identity-api-v3.rst#get-project\n\nthe list returns all projects that the caller has access, example: X-\u003eA-\u003eB-\u003eC. If a user has get_project() permissions only in projects A and C, only them will be returned calling the subtree_as_list from X (B should not be included). That was the whole reason why we have the \"subtree_as_ids\" and \"parent_as_ids\" calls.",
